{"severity":"warning","file":"errors/copy_shared_3.march","start_line":29,"start_col":17,"end_line":29,"end_col":18,"message":"`bump` builds a new copy instead of reusing `t` in place, because `t` is used again afterwards.\nA function can update a value in place only when it holds the only reference to it; make this call the last use of `t` and `bump` reuses its memory instead of allocating.","code":"copy_shared","fix":null,"labels":[{"file":"errors/copy_shared_3.march","start_line":30,"start_col":17,"end_line":30,"end_col":18,"message":"`t` is used again here, so it is still shared when `bump` runs"}],"notes":[],"category":"COPY"}
